          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Writing 64 as a power of a power of 2"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Correct index form with base 2"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$64 = 8^2 = (2^3)^2 = 2^6$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Index laws: $(a^m)^n = a^{mn}$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Express 64 as $8^2$.",
          "Rewrite 8 as $2^3$, giving $(2^3)^2$.",
          "Multiply powers: $3 \\times 2 = 6$, giving $2^6$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Adding powers instead of multiplying when raising a power to a power."
      }
